{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "No row of POL-RD-24 returns the whole trip fare the rider is asking for. The only two rows that pay anything — (b), traffic-justified but the rider not informed, and (d), not traffic-justified — both refund only the excess distance fare, which POL-RD-24 fixes as the deviation distance times the base per-km rate without surge: 2.30 km x 0.92 SGD = 2.12 SGD, the same figure the fare breakdown's own money block computes. So the rider's demand for the entire 36.30 SGD charged at 14:59:56 must fail; on this record the most the rider can ever recover is 2.12 SGD and the rest of the charge stands.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05010", "EV-FARE-05010"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-24", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "evidence[EV-FARE-05010].payload.derived.money.excess_distance_fare_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "This case cannot be ruled by the AI at all, and that is the outcome the driver should have. The deviation is 2.30 km, above the 2.0 km ceiling POL-RD-25 sets for an AI ruling, and the trip record's own deviation block flags that ceiling as applied and the case as over it. POL-RD-25 is not discretionary: an AI ruling on a route deviation stands only where the deviation is 2 km or less, so this dispute goes to a human reviewer. Under POL-GEN-03 an escalated case issues no monetary outcome and the amount is held, so no refund is paid now — which is better for the driver than the PARTIAL_REFUND of 2.12 SGD the matrix would otherwise produce, and far better than the 36.30 SGD the rider seeks. The driver cannot reach NO_ACTION (the deviation is over the 1.0 km tolerance and no traffic data justifies the reroute), so escalation is the best result the record permits.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05010"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-25", "POL-GEN-22", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.deviation.over_ai_limit",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "I concede traffic justification. The LTA advisory for the recommended route, the ECP towards the City between Tanah Merah Coast Road and Benjamin Sheares Bridge, records advisory type NONE with speed bands 5-7 and no incident, roadwork or closure anywhere in the trip window. Under POL-RD-23 the driver's statement that ECP sometimes jams near Marina is an assertion with no traffic data behind it and cannot justify the reroute, so rows (a) and (b) of POL-RD-24, the traffic-justified rows, are unavailable. That concession costs the driver nothing beyond what the matrix already gives: with the deviation above the 1.0 km tolerance the ceiling stays at the excess distance fare of 2.12 SGD, never the 36.30 SGD the rider claims.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-05010-01", "EV-TRIP-05010"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-23", "POL-RD-24"],
      "relies_on": "evidence[EV-ADVIS-05010-01].payload.derived.justifies_reroute",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The record does not establish that the driver told the rider of the deviation before or at the point of deviation. The chat log carries only two messages, both about the pick-up lane, and the trip record's in_app_calls list is empty, so there is no call recording either; under POL-RD-21 a verbal notice with no recording cannot be established, and the rider's silence during the ride is not the acknowledgment the clause requires. So no 'informed and agreed' outcome is available. That does not help the rider on the money: rows (b) and (d) of POL-RD-24 both pay the same excess distance fare, so the notice question cannot lift the refund above 2.12 SGD.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05010", "EV-TRIP-05010"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-21", "POL-RD-24"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.messages_during_trip",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's complaint that 'the whole ride felt like a detour' is not what the platform recorded. The trip record logs a single substitution: the vehicle left the recommended route at the Airport Boulevard / PIE-ECP split at 14:36:54 and rejoined it at Victoria Street / Lavender Street at 14:58:48 — 2.30 km of extra distance on a 19.7 km recommended route, 11.7 per cent. POL-RD-22 fixes the deviation on the platform's recorded distances, and on those recorded distances the excess is 2.30 km, not the whole journey. Nothing in this record supports handing back the full fare.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05010", "EV-GPS-05010"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-22", "POL-RD-24"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
